  "Waste-reduction rule (the actual fix, not just an observation): before dispatching a full tiered research sweep, `git log --oneline <last-verified-clean-sha>..HEAD -- src convex .github/workflows` (last-verified-clean-sha = the merge commit of the most recent ITERATIONS entry whose summary reports a full clean sweep across all five tiers, findable via its cited PR #) excluding prompt_process.tsx itself. An empty result means no product-affecting file has changed since that verified-clean check, so a full re-sweep can only re-derive an identical conclusion — skip straight to a fast 2-3-sample spot-check (not a full research-agent dispatch) and either find a tier-6/7/8 candidate or log a short 'confirmed still clean, zero relevant diff since <sha>' entry. Reserve a full tiered sweep (own read + dispatched research agent) for when that diff is non-empty, since a real code change is exactly what could have introduced a fresh gap. This does not license skipping baseline verification (tsc/lint/test/build) every iteration — those are cheap and catch real regressions the diff-gate doesn't (e.g. a dependency bump); it only gates the expensive from-scratch tier 1-5 research sweep.",
